 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#resolve-the-trade-off-with-an-integrated-aeo-path"&gt;Resolve the trade-off with an integrated AEO path.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-scrunch-vs-semrush-for-aeo"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About Scrunch vs. Semrush for AEO&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Why AEO Matters in Scrunch vs. Semrush&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AEO is the practice of improving how often, and how accurately, an AI answer engine like Perplexity or ChatGPT names your brand or cites your website in its answers. Measuring AEO is a different job from tracking search rankings. Instead of ten blue links, an answer engine gives a single written response that may cite several sources or none at all, so visibility means being named or cited in that response. A tool built to measure it has to read the answers themselves rather than watch a rankings table. That’s why AEO carries its own metrics and its own tools, separate from the keyword and backlink work covered in &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/aeo-vs-seo"&gt;AEO vs. SEO&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Scrunch and Semrush both measure AEO, but they specialize in different areas. Check out the comparison table before diving into the details below.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Verification note:&lt;/strong&gt; The claims in this comparison come from each vendor’s current first-party documentation, last checked in October 2026. AEO tools change their features, coverage, and pricing often, so confirm the specifics before you buy.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Scrunch vs. Semrush on Answer Engine Coverage&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Engine count is an easy first comparison across answer engine optimization tools, and Scrunch’s list is longer. Scrunch’s documentation names nine engines it can query: ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Perplexity, Google AI Mode, Google AI Overviews, Meta AI, Microsoft Copilot, and Grok. Semrush’s AI Visibility Toolkit reaches five: ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, and AI Mode.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But engine coverage within the same tool varies by plan. Scrunch’s Core plan, at $250 per month, covers four engines (ChatGPT, Perplexity, AI Overviews, and Copilot), and the remaining five require Enterprise. Semrush divides its engines by report instead, which is where coverage type comes in.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coverage type.&lt;/strong&gt; This describes where the answers behind a metric come from. Scrunch’s visibility metrics trace to prompts you choose, gathered through browser automation or official APIs, depending on the engine. Semrush blends three sources. Prompt Tracking runs your own prompts daily on ChatGPT Search, Google AI Mode, or Gemini, desktop only. Its discovery reports query an AI prompt database that Semrush compiles from clickstream records of AI searches plus Google keyword data tied to AI Overviews. Brand Performance works from a separate repository of brand-related queries that Semrush runs through each engine, and it is the only report that covers Perplexity. Semrush describes these metrics as directional signals rather than exact counts.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prompt controls.&lt;/strong&gt; Scrunch lets you assign each prompt to one engine, several, or all, and can generate prompts from customer personas with their own geography; Core includes 125 prompts. Each Semrush Prompt Tracking target runs on one engine chosen at setup, and prompts can be typed, imported from a file, or picked from suggestions, then tagged. The toolkit alone tracks 25 prompts, and Semrush One raises the cap to 100 on Pro+. For Advanced, Semrush’s help center lists 200 prompts, while its pricing page lists unlimited prompts by quote.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Geography and language.&lt;/strong&gt; Scrunch tracks prompts in any country and language, though country-specific answers show up on engines that geolocate results, such as ChatGPT, AI Overviews, and Perplexity. Semrush Prompt Tracking supports 220+ countries and territories, while its discovery reports cover 42 countries plus a worldwide view.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run frequency.&lt;/strong&gt; Scrunch queries new prompts daily for 14 days, then every 72 hours, and a “New Response” button forces a refresh. Semrush updates Prompt Tracking and its database reports daily and Brand Performance weekly.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pro tip:&lt;/strong&gt; Get the engine list for the exact plan in your quote, not the vendor’s full roster.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;How can you verify the engines a tool actually tracks?&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;During a trial, first open the engine selector when you create a prompt. Scrunch’s free trial runs on the Core plan, which includes Perplexity, Copilot, ChatGPT, and AI Overviews.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/scrunch-vs-semrush-2-20261027-1638710.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="Scrunch new prompt template dialog showing platform selection for ChatGPT, Copilot, Perplexity, AI Overviews"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p style="text-align: center; font-size: 11px; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://scrunch.com/"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Source&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Second, point one prompt at a non-US market and confirm the s...

&lt;p&gt;It’s hard to believe anything could rival Google’s impact on our digital lives and habits, but ChatGPT is on its tail — especially now that it shows ads.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For many marketers and businesses, this means debating ChatGPT Ads vs Google Search Ads for the first time. Should you move budget from Google Search ads to ChatGPT ads?&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=fbcf2b0b-3c92-4b5b-aee9-f9baf59d9721&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Download Now: Ultimate Google Ads PPC Guide [Free Kit]" height="58" width="522" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/fbcf2b0b-3c92-4b5b-aee9-f9baf59d9721.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Short answer: Not without more data, you’d better not.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;ChatGPT and Google Ads work in different ways. On Google, you bid on keywords, and Google surfaces your ad on those results pages. On ChatGPT, &lt;a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001207-ads-in-chatgpt-the-basics"&gt;OpenAI matches ads to the conversation’s&lt;/a&gt; context, and visibility isn’t guaranteed. Which fits better depends on your goals, your buyers, and how well you can measure results.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This guide unpacks five key differences to help you compare ChatGPT Ads vs Google Search Ads for your needs, and also share a decision matrix and simple hybrid test to try with your team.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note: ChatGPT ads are still in beta. Every claim below is current as of publication and linked to documentation from OpenAI, Google, or HubSpot, but things change quickly. Make sure to double-check any information before taking action.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
