&lt;h2&gt;Profound vs Peec AI: At a Glance&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Here’s how Profound, Peec AI, and HubSpot AEO stack up on the most important deciding criteria. Values reflect each vendor’s published information as of October 2026; if you want a baseline before committing to any tool, the free &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/ai-search-grader"&gt;AI Search Grader&lt;/a&gt; scores how answer engines currently represent your brand.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fit Summaries&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profound&lt;/strong&gt; fits enterprise teams that need broad engine coverage and log-level crawler data and can absorb custom Enterprise pricing to get it.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Peec AI&lt;/strong&gt; fits marketing teams and agencies that want focused, multi-country visibility tracking with unlimited seats at a lower entry price.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/strong&gt; fits teams that want an affordable entry into AEO with recommendations they can act on inside HubSpot.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Not sure where you stand today? HubSpot’s free &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/ai-search-grader"&gt;AI Search Grader&lt;/a&gt; scores how ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Gemini currently describe your brand.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What Each Platform Is Built For&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Profound, Peec AI, and HubSpot AEO all track answer-engine visibility, but each is built around a different job.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Profound: Enterprise&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core purpose:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.tryprofound.com"&gt;Profound&lt;/a&gt; sits at the enterprise-grade end of the category. It pairs deep AI-search analytics with content execution, positioning itself as what the company calls a “read/write” system for AI search rather than a reporting dashboard alone.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Typical buyer: &lt;/strong&gt;Profound’s typical buyer is an enterprise growth team, a dedicated AEO strategist, a brand or PR lead, or an agency running large client portfolios.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflow depth: &lt;/strong&gt;Profound’s workflow goes deep with server-side bot-crawl tracking, consumer prompt-demand research, up to nine tracked engines on Enterprise, and drag-and-drop agents that connect to enterprise CMS platforms.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team maturity: &lt;/strong&gt;Profound’s depth suits mature organizations that run formal AEO programs and need log-level crawler data plus enterprise security controls like SOC 2 Type II, HIPAA, and SSO.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Peec AI: Lean and Mid-Market&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core purpose:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://peec.ai"&gt;Peec AI&lt;/a&gt; answers the “what is Peec AI” question simply: It is a focused AI search analytics tool that tracks brand visibility, average position, sentiment, share of voice, and source citations across AI models, with a &lt;a href="https://docs.peec.ai/content-optimization"&gt;content optimization workspace&lt;/a&gt; for revising individual pages.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Typical buyer: &lt;/strong&gt;Peec AI’s typical buyer is a lean marketing team, an SEO or content manager, or a growth agency that wants clean multi-country tracking without paying per seat.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflow depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Peec AI’s workflow centers on measurement: Teams pick engines, tag prompts by funnel stage or persona, and read visibility trends from its dashboards. Any page an Action flags can then be reworked in a built-in editor.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team maturity:&lt;/strong&gt; Peec AI fits lean to mid-sized teams and agencies that already own their content workflow elsewhere and want an affordable, flexible reporting layer on top.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Where HubSpot AEO Fits in This Comparison&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot AEO is the affordable entry point here. Starting at &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;$50/month&lt;/a&gt;, it tracks how ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Gemini describe your brand and returns prioritized recommendations for closing the gaps it finds.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/profound-vs-peec-ai-1-20261020-3089643.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="HubSpot AEO interface showing search strategy tabs, prompt list, and recommendations panel for email hosting visibility gaps"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p style="text-align: center; font-size: 12px;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Source&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;What separates it from a measurement-only tool is context: &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/marketing/aeo"&gt;AEO in Marketing Hub&lt;/a&gt; connects to HubSpot Smart CRM so prompt suggestions reflect your own contacts, deals, and target segments rather than generic category guesses, and marketers can act on those recommendations by drafting and publishing content i...

&lt;p&gt;Buyers now ask ChatGPT, Gemini, and Perplexity for recommendations before they ever open a search results page, and marketers need a way to see whether their brand shows up in those answers. That’s why Profound vs Semrush for AEO lands on so many shortlists.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Profound and Semrush are two software companies that both help marketing teams track how their brand appears in AI-generated answers, and this guide compares them side by side. We’ll also cover a third option, &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt;, for teams after&amp;nbsp;the neutral comparison.&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;You’ll find both tools compared on engine coverage, prompt intelligence, crawler analytics, workflows, pricing, and team fit, followed by conditional verdicts so you can match a tool to your team. Search is &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/adapting-to-the-new-era-of-search"&gt;adapting to a new era&lt;/a&gt;, and picking the wrong measurement tool means paying for depth you won’t use or missing data you need.&lt;/p&gt; 
